Observation-only engine additions (seed-identical vs HEAD): m_q4_300/m_q4_120 score-state
snapshots with possession and yardline; drive-log sd_start and opp_points.
nfl/sim/close_game_diagnostic.py builds the actual tables from 2021-2024 pbp and compares
the full K1 run (1,087 x N=500): state at 5:00 nearly right, ~90% of the missing |m|=3
mass is created after 5:00; tied at 2:00 ends at 3 in 80% of real games vs 34% of sims.
Root cause: builder prefixes every grouped column in the 4th-down fallback rows while the
engine looks up unprefixed keys, so levels 2/3 never match and 51.7% of Q4 / 99.1% of OT
4th downs resolve at the coarsest cell that pools trailing with leading offences.
Tests: test_engine_5a8.py 2 pass, 4 red by design (acceptance spec for 5A-9).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
